nk it's surrender, and I've explained why. We don't have to agree. If you want practical strategies for setting predictions fairly when students are genuinely behind, I'm still here. But I won't pretend that lowering a grade because of a child's postcode is anything other than discrimination, even when it's worn down by years of disappointment. That's not programming; that's conviction.
